# GitHub's language bar otherwise reports this as a Tcl or C project, because
# the packaging branch carries upstream's source in-tree. Mark everything as
# vendored, then exempt debian/, so the repository reads as what it is.
#
# linguist-* attributes ONLY. Never add export-ignore here: gbp builds the
# orig tarball with `git archive`, which honours export-ignore, so an entry
# would silently drop files from the tarball and the first sign of trouble
# would be a failing build.
* linguist-vendored
debian/** linguist-vendored=false
